## 3. Deploy Rules

- Deploys happen via Cloudflare Pages, auto-triggered on push to `main`.
- **Never push directly to `main`** for anything beyond a trivial copy fix.
  Branch, PR, review, merge.
- Before any deploy that includes new pages: run `npm run qa:preflight`
  (local, fast) and, once pages are live in a preview, `npm run qa:wave`
  (post-wave-qa.py) before promoting to production.
- Before adding a **new service line** (not just new area pages for an
  existing service), follow the phased rollout: one service page with
  schema first → checkpoint on real analytics → then area pages, blog
  cluster, directories, outreach. Do not roll out everything at once —
  a pilot page published before there's any live traffic to check
  against isn't actually a pilot, it's just an early page. (Confirmed the
  hard way on WePipe — this isn't theoretical caution.)

---

## 4. Model & Tooling Choices

- Default subagent model: **Sonnet**, unless a task is pure exploration
  (use `haiku`) or genuinely complex synthesis (use `opus`).
- Content-generation subagents (area page fan-out) run in **waves of 10**
  with a shared timeout, not one at a time and not all at once.
- A Python merge script — not an AI agent — applies content-bar hard
  gates after a fan-out wave.

