## 6. Session Triggers

These are named, listed procedures — not something to remember. Run them
by name.

### "Starting new session"
1. Pull the latest code
2. Run `npm run qa:preflight` (catches file-level corruption before you build on it)
3. Refresh analytics if a connector is available (GA4 / GSC)
4. Check `wiki/inbox/` for dropped notes
5. Read `wiki/active-priorities.md`
6. Run the **`briefing`** skill (`start` mode) before asking what to work
   on — a spoken-style plain-language status update, not a file, not a
   bullet dump of the wiki. See `~/.claude/skills/briefing/SKILL.md`.
7. Then ask what to work on

### "Process the inbox"
Read every raw note/screenshot in `wiki/inbox/`. Extract the insight (a
long note becomes two bullets). File it on the correct wiki page. Archive
the source. Capture stays frictionless; organizing happens on demand, not
automatically.

### "End session" / "wrap up"
1. Update `wiki/active-priorities.md`
2. Append a dated entry to `SESSION-LOG.md` — what was done, deploy
   status, what's next
3. Run the **`briefing`** skill (`wrap-up` mode) — same tool as session
   start, looking backward instead of forward. Don't just restate the
   SESSION-LOG bullet list verbatim — this is for a human, not a machine.
4. Push everything immediately, so the next session sees current state

