## 7. Content & Data Standards

### Town / service data file schema (if this client needs local-area pages)

Every town data entry must include, at minimum:

```json
{
  "slug": "example-town",
  "name": "Example Town",
  "county": "Example County",
  "introDirectAnswer": "40-60 word answer-first paragraph",
  "introParagraph1": "~1,500 chars — real neighborhoods, housing stock, 10+ named local entities",
  "introParagraph2": "~1,500 chars — a first-hand practitioner voice + adjacent-town cross-link",
  "faqs": [
    { "q": "How much does [service] cost in [town]?", "a": "..." },
    { "q": "How long does [service] take?", "a": "..." },
    { "q": "What does [service] cover?", "a": "..." },
    { "q": "Who performs the work?", "a": "..." }
  ],
  "nearbyAreas": ["adjacent-town-1", "adjacent-town-2"]
}
```

**Hard rules:**
- Minimum 4 evergreen FAQs (cost / scope / timing / who-performs) at
  fixed positions, then 4–8 town-specific
- 15+ named local entities in the main narrative — regenerate if under 10
- Below ~750 characters of unique narrative per page = doorway-page risk.
  Reject.
- Exact-match verbatim phrase for the trust claim ({{define this client's
  version once finalized}}) — this is the one string allowed to repeat
  identically across every page. Everything else must be genuinely
  different per town.

### Every town slug must exist in all parallel data files.
Run `site-coverage-index.py` before proposing new pages to confirm no
duplicate pages or duplicate content under varied slugs.

